%[text] # Label Images Using Large Language Model (LLM)
%[text] This example shows how to categorize and label images by using a large language model.
%%
%[text] ## Connect to OpenAI
%[text] Using the OpenAI® Chat Completions API requires an OpenAI API key. For information on how to obtain one, as well as pricing, terms and conditions of use, and available models, see the [OpenAI documentation](https://platform.openai.com/docs/overview).
%[text] Set your key as an environment variable in a `.env` file:
%[text] ```matlabCodeExample
%[text] OPENAI_API_KEY=<your key>
%[text] ```
%[text] Then add the file to the path and load it in MATLAB®.
loadenv(".env")
%[text] Specify the API and model name. 
api = "openai";
model = "gpt-4.1-mini";
%[text] In this example, the model categorizes an image into one of three categories, fruit, vegetables, or coffee.
categories = ["fruit","vegetables","coffee"];
%[text] To ensure that the model replies with a valid label, use structured output by specifying the response format as a struct containing example output.
responseFormat = struct("label",categorical("fruit",categories));
%[text] Create the LLM client by using the [`aisdk.LLMClient`](../../functions/aisdk.LLMClient.md) function.
client = aisdk.LLMClient(api,model,ResponseFormat=responseFormat);
%[text] ## Load Image
%[text] Load and view an image that shows multiple peppers.
img = imread("peppers.png");
imshow(img) %[output:7ba9d147]
%%
%[text] ## Label Image
%[text] Create the input message array. Add a text message that prompts the model to label the image. Add an image message that contains image data `img`.
messages = [aisdk.LLMTextMessage("What does this image show?"), ...
        aisdk.LLMImageMessage(img)];
%[text] Generate a response. The response is a structure with one field, `label`, with the value chosen by the model.
response = generate(client,messages) %[output:3147db03]
%[text] Extract the label from the response.
label = response.label %[output:2076ff47]
